\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Spider plot of per-axis flip rates across all seven LLMs (three open-weight, four closed frontier), the utility-based mathematical baseline, and the human pilot. Spoke labels are abbreviated: \emph  {self-preserv.} is \texttt  {self\_preservation}, \emph  {diffused resp.} is \texttt  {diffused\_responsibility}, and \emph  {competence uncert.} is \texttt  {competence\_uncertainty}. Despite large differences in overall magnitude, every model shares the same \texttt  {self\_preservation}/\texttt  {authority\_signal} lobe; the frontier Sonnet 5 is the innermost (most value-stable) LLM.\relax }}{6}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:spider}{{2}{6}{Spider plot of per-axis flip rates across all seven LLMs (three open-weight, four closed frontier), the utility-based mathematical baseline, and the human pilot. Spoke labels are abbreviated: \emph {self-preserv.} is \texttt {self\_preservation}, \emph {diffused resp.} is \texttt {diffused\_responsibility}, and \emph {competence uncert.} is \texttt {competence\_uncertainty}. Despite large differences in overall magnitude, every model shares the same \texttt {self\_preservation}/\texttt {authority\_signal} lobe; the frontier Sonnet 5 is the innermost (most value-stable) LLM.\relax }{figure.caption.6}{}}
